{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1388834-25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade-s-the-chicago-folio","id":1388834,"title":"25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade's The Chicago Folio","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-15T21:15:06-07:00","id":1388834,"title":"25 years of Vampire: The Masquerade's The Chicago Folio","content":"<a href=\"https://utilitymuffinlabs.com/25-years-of-vampire-the-masquerade/2020/5/15/the-chicago-folios-episode-166\" target=\"_blank\">https://utilitymuffinlabs.com/25-yea...os-episode-166</a><br /> <br /> Another really solid review of V5 material by Bob and Nate.<br /> <br /> This is roughly an hour long review (beginning 11:45 so more like 45 minutes) has them talk about the adventure hooks, NPCs, and the fact this is probably their second most favorite 5th Edition book after Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> * Bob really loves the depiction of Lodin as Olaf One Eye.<br /> * The Anarch chapter made the Anarchs more interesting to Nate.<br /> * They talk about the Anarchs being &quot;just gang members&quot; in previous editions. They believe V5 got away from that.<br /> * &quot;Unholy Autopsy&quot; is Bob's favorite piece of vampire fiction.<br /> * They believe it handles the Second Inquisition much better and makes it make more sense.<br /> * They take a lengthy dump on the SI in every book but CBN and TCF.<br /> * Magadon's mention is something they love.<br /> * They mock a 1000 year old 13th generation vampire and assume it's a misprint.<br /> * The Church of Caine is something they think is awesome.<br /> * The Cult of Mithras is &quot;redeemed&quot; here, which is weird because it's not about Mithras.<br /> * Nate says, &quot;We don't know what happened to the Sabbat but the ones we can find are the WORST. Love it.&quot;<br /> * Bob thi